//! Named-view help (V12).

pub(super) const HELP: &str = "Model views (V12): named views with their own view plane and display properties, kept in a session JSON file beside the model; the store is never written. list-views --file FILE returns the folders and every view. rename-view-folder --file FILE --from PATH --to PATH renames (or moves) a folder with its subfolders and views; remove-view-folder --file FILE --name PATH removes a folder and keeps its contents, which move up into its parent. save-view --file FILE [--name NAME] creates a view from exactly one plane: an orbit --yaw RAD --pitch RAD [--target X,Y,Z]; a coordinate plane --parallel xy|xz|yz [--offset MM]; an explicit frame --plane OX,OY,OZ,XX,XY,XZ,YX,YY,YZ; --two-points A;B (vertical, or across the input plane given by --work-plane); --three-points A;B;C; or, reading the model through --store ROOT: --grid SELECTOR --axis LABEL (one axis) or --grid SELECTOR [--u-axes none|first|last|all] [--v-axes ...] [--u-prefix TEXT] [--v-prefix TEXT] (one view per axis, named prefix and label), --level NAME|ID or --levels first|last|all, --element ID or --assembly ID with --side front|back|top|bottom|end|3d|four (four creates front, top, end and 3d), and --ray-origin X,Y,Z --ray-direction X,Y,Z [--edge A;B] (the first face hit). Without --name a single view is named View N (the lowest free number) and a batch by its labels alone. Batches add all views or none and suffix repeated names. save-view may stamp provenance --author TEXT [--comment TEXT], which needs --store ROOT: every created view then records the author, the save time, the comment and the model revision it was captured against (update-view never rewrites the stamp). Display properties, for save-view and update-view: --projection, --span MM (visible height), --depth none|ABOVE,BELOW (distance shown towards the viewer and behind the plane), --rotation Z_DEG,X_DEG (turns the camera, not the plane), --render-mode, --grids, --hidden-kinds none|KIND,..., --work-area none|six numbers, --color default|R,G,B (0..1), --opacity 0..1, --folder PATH, --favorite, --default true|false (the one default view of the model: setting it moves the mark, and the default view cannot be removed or unmarked), --copy-from VIEW. update-view --file FILE --view ID|NAME [--name NEW] changes one view, its plane through any single-view option. remove-view and apply-view take --view ID|NAME; apply-view returns the view, its provenance, its camera frame and its clip planes, without touching any store. Discipline view presets (V07) are a named bundle of the display components only: the kind filter (whose reference kind is the reference visibility), the underlay depth slab above and below the plane, the representation level, the name of a saved colour set, the grid toggle and the view filter overrides; a preset holds no camera and no provenance, so applying one never touches a store or the snapshot token. define-preset --file FILE --name TEXT [--hidden-kinds none|KIND,...] [--depth none|ABOVE,BELOW] [--representation full|simplified] [--colour-set none|NAME] [--grids true|false] [--overrides none|SPEC;...] defines one in the preset file (personal configuration, a bounded versioned JSON document; a missing file is an empty book). list-presets --file FILE lists them, remove-preset --file FILE --name TEXT removes one, and apply-preset --file FILE --views-file VIEWSFILE --preset NAME --view ID|NAME writes the bundle onto one saved view (the camera, the render mode, the colour, the opacity, the folder and the provenance stay) and rewrites the views file in its canonical layer form. save-view and update-view also take --representation and --colour-set to set the two view fields on their own. View filters live in the views file beside the camera prims, and each view keeps its filter overrides. list-view-filters --file FILE returns the filters. save-view-filter --file FILE --name NAME [--rename-from OLD] [--match all|any] [--conditions none|ROW;...] adds or changes a filter; a ROW is `field op value` with field type, name, class or attribute:NAME and op eq, ne, lt, le, gt, ge, contains or starts-with, for example `type eq beam;class ge 2`; a rename follows into every view. remove-view-filter --file FILE --name NAME removes it and every override that names it. save-view and update-view take --overrides none|SPEC;... (a SPEC is `filter|show or hide|R,G,B or -|transparency`, the first matching override decides how an element is drawn); a preset's overrides must name filters of the views file it is applied in.";
